; THE AES_192 KEY SCHEDULE  fifty two words from six  into a buffer;
;
; FIPS 197 section 5 point 2 with Nk of six and Nr of twelve; Word i is
; w at i minus six exclusive ored with temp  where temp is w at i minus one;
; every SIXTH word puts temp through RotWord then SubWord then the round
; constant  and every other word is taken as it stands; There is no second
; transform rule here; that one belongs to Nk of eight alone  and its
; absence is the only thing in this file that an Nk of eight reader has to
; look twice at;
;
; SIX STATIC SLOTS AND NO SHIFTING  which is aes/keyexpand128's argument at
; a wider key: the schedule only ever wants w at i minus Nk and w at i
; minus one  so an Nk word window is enough  and because the group of six
; words is written ONCE and looped  word i lives in slot i mod six and the
; slot each step touches is a constant in the text;
;
; FORTY SIX WORDS IS SEVEN GROUPS AND A PART ONE; seven turns of the
; loop make forty two and the last four are written out below it; That is
; the same shape aes/encrypt128 has for its tenth round  and for the same
; reason: a loop whose last turn differs is two pieces of text  not a flag;
;
; THE BUFFER IS A CONVEYOR; each new word slides the two hundred and eight
; cells one word to the left and lands at the tail  so nothing is ever
; addressed by a computed offset and the words come to rest in order; Fifty two
; appends at two hundred and four moves is a few million instructions
; which against this file's work is a small part  and against the cipher
; that consumes it is nothing;
;
; WHY A BUFFER AT ALL  when aes/keyexpand128 emits each word as it is made:
; because a CIPHER cannot read its own standard output; aes/keyexpand192
; includes this and emits the buffer  and the ciphers include it and consume
; the buffer from the front; One schedule  two uses  and the published
; vectors of the program are what pin the ciphers' copy of it;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset resolves them;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x000:0x018  the paste workspace; aes/xorword reaches 0 to 24 and
;                 aes/xtime 0 to 21; every paste sits at this block's zero
;   @0x019:0x030  window{24}  six slots of four; slot s at 25 plus 4s
;   @0x039:0x03c  temp{4}   w at i minus one  worked on in place
;   @0x03d        rcon      the round constant
;   @0x03e        g         the cell a copy hands its value back through
;   @0x072:0x074  group 0 of the walk; ITS TRAIL IS NEVER SET
;   @0x075:0x372  groups 1 to 256  the S box  LAID BY THE CALLER
;   @0x37a        cnt  groups of six still to do
;   @0x380:0x383  the word being appended; it ABUTS the buffer because
;                 block/rkappend208 lays the buffer at its own plus four
;   @0x384:0x453  the fifty two words  in order  once this block is done
;
; THE ENTRY CLAIM NAMES ONLY THE CELLS THIS BLOCK OWNS  and that is not
; fussiness; it used to read "zero from temp to the end of the buffer"  which
; was true of the schedule PROGRAM and false of every cipher: by the time a
; cipher includes this  the S box is laid at 117 and the plaintext is in the
; state at 82  and the claim failed on the table's first datum and then on
; the plaintext's second byte; A block may only make claims about its own
; frame  and the cells between are the CALLER's business;
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; ASSERT zero +57:+62
; ASSERT zero +890:+890
; ASSERT zero +896:+899
; ASSERT zero +900:+1107

